<!DOCTYPE html><html data-dpl-id="dpl_DypmBSbT9yEBcUR7LC2Sz3ssCvYe" lang="en"><head><meta charSet="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><link rel="stylesheet" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3lg58otdl8my-.css" data-precedence="next"/><link rel="preload" as="script" fetchPriority="low" href="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ddg70z30qn04.js"/><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/41b5e_o-w2xun.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1cmnso0jnkwt6.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/2-k_577svdq9-.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/turbopack-2l6qdc9b47pt9.js" async=""></script><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js" async="" crossorigin=""></script><title>Documentation · MCPCN</title><meta name="description" content="React components and workflow blocks for human-controlled MCP Apps."/><link rel="icon" href="/icon.svg?icon.0-2l4nus4v8l3.svg" sizes="any" type="image/svg+xml"/><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/0c0hxoamwjsbw.js" noModule=""></script></head><body><div hidden=""><!--$--><!--/$--></div><header class="site-nav"><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark">M</span>MCPCN</a><nav><a href="/docs">Docs</a><a href="/components">Components</a><a href="/blocks">Blocks</a><a href="/examples">Examples</a><a href="/playground">Playground</a></nav><div class="nav-actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/create">Create</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui" class="button">GitHub</a></div></header><main class="docs-layout"><aside class="sidebar" aria-label="Documentation sections"><strong>Getting started</strong><a href="#contract">The contract</a><a href="#install">Install</a><a href="#provider">Mount your provider</a><a href="#first-component">Your first component</a><a href="#host-compatibility">Host compatibility</a><a href="#security-boundaries">Security boundaries</a><a href="#registry">Registry</a><a href="#server-helpers">Server helpers</a></aside><article class="prose" style="min-width:0"><span class="eyebrow">Documentation</span><h1>Build a reviewable agent workflow</h1><p>MCPCN connects structured MCP tool results to React review surfaces. Your application handles user actions and validates every operation on the server.</p><h2 id="contract">The contract</h2><pre class="code">Tool structuredContent
  → validate the payload and component schema
  → render a typed component or a safe error
  → user reviews and acts
  → your application calls a permitted tool
  → render the updated result</pre><h2 id="install">Install into an existing React app</h2><p role="status"><strong>Package release pending.</strong> The npm packages and executable are not published yet. The commands below describe the prepared source interface for a forthcoming release.</p><p>The installer prepares TypeScript files and configuration. It does not create a framework app, install dependencies automatically or establish a host connection.</p><h3>Own the source</h3><p>Copy components, schemas, runtime and shared styles into your app. Workflow blocks include their component dependencies. Review the files and install the reported consumer dependencies yourself.</p><pre class="code">pnpm dlx mcpcn init --mode=copy --style=default --host=auto --manager=pnpm --components-dir=components/mcpcn --registry=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/main/registry/items
pnpm dlx mcpcn add review-before-action
pnpm add &#x27;zod@^4.4.0&#x27; @modelcontextprotocol/ext-apps@1.7.5 @modelcontextprotocol/sdk@1.30.0</pre><h3>Use package imports</h3><p>Keep component imports in the MCPCN packages and generate your local provider. The component selection determines the import instructions; the dependency command installs the shared packages.</p><pre class="code">pnpm dlx mcpcn init --mode=package --style=default --host=auto --manager=pnpm --components-dir=components/mcpcn --registry=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/main/registry/items
pnpm dlx mcpcn add approval-card
pnpm add @mcpcn/react @mcpcn/runtime @mcpcn/schemas @mcpcn/themes</pre><p><a href="/create">Configure a different manager, theme, host or selection.</a> Both modes require an existing React application. JavaScript output is not supported by this source installer.</p><h2 id="provider">Mount your provider</h2><p>The generated <code>components/mcpcn<!-- -->/provider.tsx</code> applies your chosen theme and creates the selected adapter on the client. Mount <code>MCPCNProvider</code> around your MCP App UI. Import paths in these examples are relative to your project root; adjust them to the location of your integration file.</p><pre class="code">&quot;use client&quot;;

import { useEffect, useState, type ReactNode } from &quot;react&quot;;
import { AgentAppProvider, detectAdapter, type AgentAppAdapter } from &quot;./_mcpcn/runtime&quot;;
import &quot;./styles.css&quot;;

export function MCPCNProvider({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  const [adapter, setAdapter] = useState&lt;AgentAppAdapter | null&gt;(null);
  useEffect(() =&gt; { setAdapter(detectAdapter()); }, []);
  return &lt;div className=&quot;mcpcn&quot; data-mcpcn-theme=&quot;default&quot;&gt;
    {adapter ? &lt;AgentAppProvider adapter={adapter}&gt;{children}&lt;/AgentAppProvider&gt;
      : &lt;p role=&quot;status&quot; aria-busy=&quot;true&quot;&gt;Preparing app connection…&lt;/p&gt;}
  &lt;/div&gt;;
}
</pre><p>Copy mode includes local styles. Package mode imports <code>@mcpcn/react/styles.css</code> and <code>@mcpcn/themes/default.css</code>. The provider sets <code>data-mcpcn-theme</code> for Default, Graphite or Violet.</p><h2 id="first-component">Your first component</h2><p>For this example, add <code>approval-card</code> using the configurator. Connect <code>onApprove</code> to your own authorized action, and provide its pending/error handling.</p><pre class="code">import { MCPCNProvider } from &quot;./components/mcpcn/provider&quot;;
import { ApprovalCard } from &quot;./components/mcpcn/approval-card&quot;;

export function ReviewAction({ onApprove }: { onApprove: () =&gt; void }) {
  return &lt;MCPCNProvider&gt;
    &lt;ApprovalCard
      title=&quot;Send this email?&quot;
      riskLevel=&quot;medium&quot;
      actionLabel=&quot;Send&quot;
      changes={[{ label: &quot;Recipients&quot;, after: &quot;43 customers&quot; }]}
      onAction={({ type }) =&gt; { if (type === &quot;approve&quot;) onApprove(); }}
    /&gt;
  &lt;/MCPCNProvider&gt;;
}</pre><h2 id="host-compatibility">Host compatibility</h2><p>Auto detect uses the existing runtime detection: OpenAI compatibility when that host surface exists, the official MCP Apps adapter inside an iframe, and a local mock otherwise. Standard MCP Apps explicitly selects <code>OfficialMCPAdapter</code>; OpenAI compatibility explicitly selects <code>OpenAIAdapter</code>. Configuration does not grant host capabilities or server permissions.</p><p>The configurator previews are authored local examples. Their actions never execute host tools or install files, and they are not a live host acceptance check.</p><h2 id="security-boundaries">Security boundaries</h2><p>A UI approval is not server authorization. Keep raw personal data in private UI or server state, send only deliberate context to the model, and validate every app-initiated tool call on the server. Treat tools, membership and destructive operations as application-owned permissions.</p><h2 id="registry">Registry</h2><p>The source registry contains component and workflow-block entries with their local source closure. Choose a registry you trust, review installed files, and retain the lockfile to detect changes before updating. The CLI reports required dependencies instead of running a package manager for you.</p><h2 id="server-helpers">Server helpers</h2><p>The separate <code>@mcpcn/server</code> helpers support MCP tool/resource registration. Client installation does not create a server, authorization policy or production endpoint. Connect your reviewed UI to an app-visible tool in your own server integration.</p><p><a href="/docs/server">Build a validated MCP server integration</a> with complete result schemas, request context, explicit private metadata and standard resource/CSP declarations.</p><a class="button" href="/components">Explore the catalog</a></article></main><!--$--><!--/$--><footer><div><strong>MCPCN</strong><p>Human control for agentic apps.</p></div><div><a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui">GitHub</a><a href="https://github.com/alvarovillalbaa/mcpcn-ui/blob/main/SECURITY.md">Security</a></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ddg70z30qn04.js" id="_R_" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:\"$Sreact.fragment\"\n2:I[14058,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"\"]\n3:I[43820,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n4:I[98737,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\"]\n24:I[98025,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\"],\"default\",1]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3lg58otdl8my-.css\",\"style\"]\n22:X\n0:{\"P\":null,\"c\":[\"\",\"docs\"],\"q\":\"\",\"i\":false,\"f\":[[[\"\",{\"children\":[\"docs\",{\"children\":[\"__PAGE__\",{},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4608]},\"$undefined\",\"$undefined\",4624],[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3lg58otdl8my-.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}],[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/29nm6-6cbu5hi.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"site-nav\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"href\":\"/\",\"className\":\"brand\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"brand-mark\",\"children\":\"M\"}],\"MCPCN\"]}],[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/docs\",{\"href\":\"/docs\",\"children\":\"Docs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/components\",{\"href\":\"/components\",\"children\":\"Components\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/blocks\",{\"href\":\"/blocks\",\"children\":\"Blocks\"}],[\"$\",\"$L2\",\"/examples\",{\"href\":\"/examples\",\"children\":\"Examples